2049	 *
2050	 * 'u' contains n * 1/prime[]
2051	 * 'r' is filled with 16x16-bit result
2052	 *     ffff  entry in prime[] divides n  OR  divides 2n+1
2053	 *        0  prime[] is not a factor
2054	 * 'r' and 'u' may point to the same memory; MUST NOT overlap with 'tmp'
2055	 *
2056	 * 'tmp' is centralized scratch, filled with (potentially)secret-dependent data
2057	 *
2058	 * TODO: check whether storing 2/p[] is more efficient than 2*(1/p)
